# ── Single Cloudflare Pages project · shared deploy for the remaining sites ──
# One project (digimax) still serves admin.* and creatives.* on top of the
# main storefront — see CONSOLIDATION.md. marketing.* and agentic.* have been
# extracted to their own lean, standalone Cloudflare Pages projects
# (dsm-marketing / dsm-agentic-services) and are no longer part of this build;
# their custom domains + DNS point straight at those projects now, so no
# host-based rule for them is needed here anymore.
#
# Rule order matters: the "already-prefixed" passthrough for admin must come
# before its catch-all, so a request that already carries the real path
# (e.g. an absolute /admin/assets/... asset request) isn't double-prefixed by
# the catch-all underneath it.

# Admin — admin.digitalsoftwaremarket.ai. admin-app's own asset refs are
# absolute (/admin/...), so those already resolve directly against the shared
# deployment; only bare/deep paths need falling back to the app shell.
https://admin.digitalsoftwaremarket.ai/admin/*        /admin/:splat            200
https://admin.digitalsoftwaremarket.ai/*              /admin/index.html        200

# Creatives — creatives.digitalsoftwaremarket.ai falls through to the normal
# SPA fallback below (no rule needed here): App.tsx detects this hostname at
# runtime and renders the existing RegisteredCreatives page ("/creatives")
# as the "/" route for this host only, while every other route (/store,
# /cart, /account, ...) stays available via ordinary in-app client routing.

# Admin SPA (built from admin-app/ under /admin) — must come BEFORE the store fallback.
/admin/*              /admin/index.html                200

# The marketing + services (DSM AI Labs / agentic) microsites are now fully
# standalone deployments — nothing real is left under /marketing or /services
# in this build anymore (2026-09-24: the last 50+ static service pages moved
# out to dsm-agentic-services too). Wildcard every old path across, so every
# bookmarked/linked sub-page (offerings.html, the generated service pages,
# case studies, etc.) redirects to its new home instead of 404ing in the SPA.
/marketing/*          https://marketing.digitalsoftwaremarket.ai/:splat   302
/services/*           https://agentic.digitalsoftwaremarket.ai/:splat     302

# SPA fallback for the React store / landing (every other client route).
/*                    /index.html                      200
